      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "white",
        "eyebrow": "The house",
        "statement": "In India, a flower is never only a flower. It is a greeting, a blessing, a thing you give when words are not enough.",
        "text": "<p>Florève begins with that idea. In marigold at a doorway, jasmine in the hair, petals offered with both hands — the flower carries feeling, and it has done so for as long as anyone can remember.</p><p>We take that meaning and give it an Italian discipline of line: reduced, balanced, nothing ornamental for its own sake. What remains is shaped by hand, slowly, with the care the original gesture deserves.</p>",
        "link_label": "Our story",
        "padding_top": 112,
        "padding_bottom": 96
      }
    },
